-- SHADOW-SEMANTICS cell I11: an importer shadow of a PRELUDE method (i4's
-- shape) whose live-impl receiver is EXTERN-SOURCED.
--
-- 🚨 THE POINT OF THIS CELL IS THE RECEIVER'S PROVENANCE, NOT ITS TYPE, and
-- that is this gate's own ⭐ rule ("vary the receiver's PROVENANCE — literal /
-- grounded / dict-bound — that axis is where every silent bug in this arc has
-- lived").  Lines 2 and 3 below have the SAME receiver type, `Int`, reached two
-- different ways: an annotated literal, and the result of an `extern`.  Every
-- other fixture in this corpus uses an annotated or literal receiver, so the
-- corpus graded 36/36 over the break this cell pins.
--
-- WHAT IT PINS.  `stdlib/runtime.mdk`'s extern signatures never pass through
-- resolve's head-stamping walk, so a mono flowing out of one carries no
-- `TyConOrigin`.  The importer rule (Fork 1) is "a live impl at the receiver's
-- head dispatches, else the standalone", and the head here is `Int` on both
-- lines — so all four answers are fixed by the head TYPE alone and provenance
-- must not enter into it.  A dispatch site that compares the goal head's
-- IDENTITY against the impl head's answers False for lines 3 and 4 only, and
-- silently reroutes them to the imported standalone `display : Tok -> String`
-- (`implExistsForHeadGo`, `compiler/types/typecheck.mdk`).
--
-- HAND-DERIVED, not captured:
--   `display (Tok 0)`             Tok has NO Display impl  -> the standalone -> tok
--   `display (3 : Int)`           live prelude Display Int -> the METHOD     -> 3
--   `display (stringLength "xy")` same head, same impl                       -> 2
--   `display (charCode 'a')`      same head, same impl                       -> 97
import prov.{Tok(..), display}

main =
  println (display (Tok 0))
  println (display (3 : Int))
  println (display (stringLength "xy"))
  println (display (charCode 'a'))
